lication/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Verify attestation — `[non-codebase]` AC\n\n**The verify suite is green for this change. CI exit status: SUCCESS (0).**\n\n- Change: Gerrit 2991, patch set 1, revision `2ddf76f60adecdc40d94ea1f4b17953a0dcacdc0`\n- CI run: https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/35488606407\n- Verdict: `rebar-ci-bot` cast **`Verified +1` — SUCCESS**, every job green (lint +\n  type-check, the `ubuntu-latest, py3.13` gating pytest cell and the rest of the matrix,\n  sandbox enforcement, mutation, artifact-probe, authorship, optionality,\n  scanner-integration).\n- Landed: submitted revision-scoped and merged to `main`.\n\n`AGENTS.md` defines `make test` as selecting exactly what CI's gating `ubuntu-latest, py3.13`\ncell selects, and describes a local `make verify` as \"the locally checkable **half** of\n`Verified`\". CI ran that selection plus the rest of the matrix and passed, so this is the\nstronger of the two signals.","timestamp":1789882733009959545}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788609221095072001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7d068668-615c-48d9-826d-5aaf1f91b7bc","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"aacb-cceb-01e9-46b3"},{"link_uuid":"0bb6a62f-8311-4a8c-9e20-543752b8ee94","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"395b-a59a-c732-4d1d"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`.github/llm-providers/README.md:3-5` says each `REBAR_LLM_CONFIG_FILE` provider overlay sets `only` `[llm.model_classes]`, repoints the 3 model classes, and changes nothing else. `.github/llm-providers/README.md:11-13` says `tests/unit/test_ci_provider_matrix.py` fails if an overlay sets anything outside `[llm.model_classes]`. Those statements no longer match the current tree.\n\nThe committed overlays contain exactly one top-level `[llm]` table with both a scalar `model` and a nested `model_classes` table: `.github/llm-providers/openai.toml:8-14`, `.github/llm-providers/anthropic.toml:8-14`, and `.github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml:14-20`. The scalar `llm.model` is load-bearing because callers can resolve `cfg.model` outside the class table; the overlay comments record that rationale at `.github/llm-providers/openai.toml:5-7`, `.github/llm-providers/anthropic.toml:5-7`, and `.github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml:10-12`.\n\nThe parser path also differs from the README wording: `src/rebar/_config_sources.py:238-248` reads the pointed file's `[llm]` table and deep-merges it into discovered configuration. The enforcement in `tests/unit/test_ci_provider_matrix.py:134-147` asserts the top-level key set is exactly `{\"llm\"}`, the nested `[llm]` key set is exactly `{\"model\", \"model_classes\"}`, `llm.model` is provider-qualified for the matrix arm, and `model_classes` covers every class slot.\n\n## Approach\nUpdate `.github/llm-providers/README.md` to describe the actual overlay schema and the actual matrix enforcement. Retain the README's deep-merge, provider isolation, local-use, credential, and verified-model guidance. Workflow comment remediation remains owned by `sphalerite-bereft-tortoise`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `.github/llm-providers/README.md` removes the claim at lines 3-5 that each overlay sets `only` `[llm.model_classes]` and replaces it with the statement that each overlay contains one top-level `[llm]` table with `model` and `model_classes`.\n- [x] `.github/llm-providers/README.md` explains that scalar `llm.model` is required because callers can resolve `cfg.model` outside class slots, matching the overlay rationale in `.github/llm-providers/openai.toml:5-7`, `.github/llm-providers/anthropic.toml:5-7`, and `.github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml:10-12`.\n- [x] `.github/llm-providers/README.md` replaces the enforcement claim at lines 11-13 with a statement matching `tests/unit/test_ci_provider_matrix.py:134-147`: top-level keys must be exactly `{\"llm\"}`, `[llm]` keys must be exactly `{\"model\", \"model_classes\"}`, `llm.model` must be provider-qualified, and every model class slot must be present.\n- [x] `.github/llm-providers/README.md` keeps the deep-merge description aligned with `src/rebar/_config_sources.py:238-248`, where `REBAR_LLM_CONFIG_FILE` layers the pointed `[llm]` table over discovered settings instead of replacing the entire config.\n- [x] [non-codebase] The full verify suite is green for this change, with the run and its\n      exit code recorded on this ticket. The authoritative signal is the Gerrit `Verified`\n      vote on this change's patch set, which runs the same selection `make test` runs.\n      provenance: environment=github-actions-hosted-runner; principal=rebar-ci-bot; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — CI run 35488606407 executed the gating suite against Gerrit change 2991 patch set 1 (revision 2ddf76f60adecdc40d94ea1f4b17953a0dcacdc0) and concluded SUCCESS, casting `Verified +1`; that run is the same merge gate that admits the change to `main`, so its exit status is the authoritative verify result rather than a simulation of one.\n\n## Testing\nRun `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify` from the repository checkout and land only if it exits 0.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":".github/llm-providers/README.md","reason":"Correct the provider overlay schema, scalar-model rationale, deep-merge wording, and matrix enforcement claims."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","395b-a59a-c732-4d1d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"9aead2fa-7f40-4dd3-b8da-218d